<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title>Eurogamer.net Latest Articles Feed</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/feed</link><description>This is a feed of the latest articles from Eurogamer.net.</description><atom:link href="https://www.eurogamer.net/feed" rel="self"/><language>en</language><copyright>Copyright (c) Eurogamer.net a brand of IGN Entertainment, Inc.</copyright><lastBuildDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 19:44:16 +0000</lastBuildDate><item><title>Marvel Tōkon: Fighting Souls dev apologises for PC "gameplay and performance issues"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/marvel-tokon-fighting-souls-pc-beta-apology</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 19:44:16 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/marvel-tokon-fighting-souls-pc-beta-apology</guid><category>Marvel Games</category><category>PS5</category><category>performance</category><category>PC</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Beta</category><category>Side view</category><category>Arc System Works</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Fighting</category><category>Marvel Tokon: Fighting Souls</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/MARVEL-T%C5%8Dkon-3.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/MARVEL-T%C5%8Dkon-3.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The open beta for Marvel T&omacr;kon: Fighting Souls is finally here, and it seems PC players are struggling with a host of issues unique to the PC port, prompting developer Arc System Works to issue an apology and troubleshooting guidelines over the weekend.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/marvel-tokon-fighting-souls-pc-beta-apology">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"Sony had the strictest social media guidelines they've ever seen issued," says former first-party dev about physical disc backlash</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-disc-backlash-no-surprise-says-former-dev</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 18:17:06 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-disc-backlash-no-surprise-says-former-dev</guid><category>Sony PlayStation</category><category>Physical Media</category><category>Social Media</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ps6-games-calendar.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ps6-games-calendar.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Sony has reportedly issued its strictest-ever social media guidelines to staff at its first-party studios following the backlash to its physical media announcement.
</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-disc-backlash-no-surprise-says-former-dev">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The next Kratos God of War game will follow and connect to Laufey, says Cory Barlog</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/kratos-god-of-war-links-directly-to-laufey</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 17:27:52 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/kratos-god-of-war-links-directly-to-laufey</guid><category>God of War Laufey</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Sony Santa Monica</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/god-of-war-laufey-classic-cover-1.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/god-of-war-laufey-classic-cover-1.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Santa Monica Studio head of creative, Cory Barlog, has confirmed that the next mainline, Kratos-starring God of War will pick up after the events of God of War Laufey.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/kratos-god-of-war-links-directly-to-laufey">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>007 First Light's first major patch is here – and it's a doozy if you're playing on PS5</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/007-first-light-first-major-patch-details</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 15:44:24 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/007-first-light-first-major-patch-details</guid><category>IO Interactive</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>patches</category><category>007 First Light</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/James-Bond-looks-sad-in-007-First-Light.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/James-Bond-looks-sad-in-007-First-Light.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>007 First Light's first major post-launch update, Patch 1.1.0, is here, introducing "fixes and improvements for over 200 issues reported by the community and our internal playtesters".</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/007-first-light-first-major-patch-details">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Wuchang: Fallen Feathers tops 5 million players despite dev team's collapse</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/wuchang-fallen-feathers-5-million-players</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 26 Jul 2026 15:05:53 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/wuchang-fallen-feathers-5-million-players</guid><category>RPG</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Leenzee Games</category><category>PS5</category><category>Wuchang: Fallen Feathers</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>RPG: Action</category><category>Single Player</category><category>game sales data</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>505 Games</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/wuchang-fallen-feathers-commander-honglan-header.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/wuchang-fallen-feathers-commander-honglan-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/wuchang-fallen-feathers">Wuchang: Fallen Feathers</a> has surpassed five million players.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/wuchang-fallen-feathers-5-million-players">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Silent Hill f writers were challenged to read "100-200 books a year" during production</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/silent-hill-f-writers-read-100-200-books-a-year-during-development</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 17:25:17 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/silent-hill-f-writers-read-100-200-books-a-year-during-development</guid><category>Development</category><category>Konami</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>writers</category><category>Puzzle</category><category>Horror</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Silent Hill f</category><category>Neobards Entertainment</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Silent_Hill_f_ending_Header.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Silent_Hill_f_ending_Header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Silent Hill producer Motoi Okamoto said the scriptwriters of <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/silent-hill-f">Silent Hill f</a> "pressured each other" to read "100 to 200 books a year", including those from f's writer Ryukishi07, to ensure they had a thorough understanding of the writer's "style and quirks".</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/silent-hill-f-writers-read-100-200-books-a-year-during-development">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Aliens: Fireteam Elite 2 confirms release date and it's closer than you think</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/aliens-fireteam-elite-2-release-date-confirmed</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 16:39:20 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/aliens-fireteam-elite-2-release-date-confirmed</guid><category>Shooter: Third Person</category><category>PS5</category><category>Science Fiction</category><category>Daybreak Game Company</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Horror</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>release dates</category><category>Aliens: Fireteam Elite 2</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Cold Iron Studios</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Screenshot-2026-07-25-at-17.25.46.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Screenshot-2026-07-25-at-17.25.46.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/aliens-fireteam">Aliens: Fireteam Elite</a> 2 will release on 25th August 2026.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/aliens-fireteam-elite-2-release-date-confirmed">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>God of War Laufey finally gets a release date - here's when you'll be able to play it</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-laufey-release-date-confirmed</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 15:28:10 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-laufey-release-date-confirmed</guid><category>God of War Laufey</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>release dates</category><category>Sony Santa Monica</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/A-peaceful-looking-Faye-in-God-of-War-Laufey.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/A-peaceful-looking-Faye-in-God-of-War-Laufey.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>God of War Laufey will release on 16th February 2027.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-laufey-release-date-confirmed">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>What we've been playing - "Gosh I had a really fun 30 minutes with Marvel Tokon before PSN went down"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/what-weve-been-playing-marvel-tokon-psn-down</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 25 Jul 2026 07:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/what-weve-been-playing-marvel-tokon-psn-down</guid><category>Social</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>Ubisoft Quebec City</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>RPG</category><category>Simulation</category><category>Android</category><category>Marvel Games</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>The Pokémon Company International</category><category>Side view</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Free-2-Play</category><category>Open World</category><category>Marvel Tokon: Fighting Souls</category><category>iOS</category><category>First person</category><category>Pokémon Go</category><category>Niantic</category><category>What we've been playing</category><category>Arc System Works</category><category>Scopely Explore</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Family-friendly</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>Assassin's Creed Odyssey</category><category>PS4</category><category>Stadia</category><category>Ubisoft</category><category>Ubisoft Entertainment</category><category>Anime</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Fighting</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Blade-ult-Marvel-Tokon.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Blade-ult-Marvel-Tokon.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Hello and welcome back to our regular feature where we write a little about the games we've been playing. This week, Bertie goes back to ancient Greece for an odyssey of his own; Kelsey goes bird watching; and Connor crosses all his fingers and toes for Sony to fix PlayStation Network.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/what-weve-been-playing-marvel-tokon-psn-down">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Lara Croft can't catch a break: after delaying one Tomb Raider game, Amazon is delaying another and this one won't show up until 2028</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/tomb-raider-catalyst-delay-2028</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Matt Wales</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 17:06:13 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/tomb-raider-catalyst-delay-2028</guid><category>Flying Wild Hog</category><category>Shooter: Third Person</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Puzzle</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Fantasy</category><category>Platformer</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis</category><category>Crystal Dynamics</category><category>Amazon Games</category><category>Tomb Raider: Catalyst</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/tomb-raider-catalyst-trailer-crop.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/tomb-raider-catalyst-trailer-crop.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Lara Croft's big comeback at the hands of Amazon has hit yet another hitch. After TV show setbacks and a delay for Tomb Raider 1 "reimagining" Legacy of Atlantis, Amazon's gaming boss has confirmed yet another delay: Lara's other adventure, Tomb Raider: Catalyst, now won't arrive until some time in 2028.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/tomb-raider-catalyst-delay-2028">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>It looks like we're getting a Halo 2 remake next, but is that really a surprise?</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/halo-2-remake-tease-legendary-ending-campaign-evolved</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 15:32:41 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/halo-2-remake-tease-legendary-ending-campaign-evolved</guid><category>First person</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Halo Studios</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Halo: Campaign Evolved</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>FPS</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Halo-2-CE.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Halo-2-CE.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Halo has a proud history of smuggling secret endings into its campaigns. In the very first 2001 game, there is a hidden (non-canon) ending featuring Sgt. Avery Johnson fighting and hugging an Elite. In <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/halo-2">Halo 2</a>, there's a mid-credits scene that teases the beginning of <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/halo-3">Halo 3</a>. In Halo 3, we get a full scene of Chief drifting, alone, in the cold, indifferent vacuum of space. ODST gives us a glimpse of the Engineers' secret. And in Reach, my personal favourite, we get that phenomenal 'Lone Wolf' ending that still sends shivers down my spine to think about today.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/halo-2-remake-tease-legendary-ending-campaign-evolved">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Amid the recent Xbox devastation, Microsoft is seemingly uncancelling something, which is good news for Age of Empires 3 fans at least</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-age-of-empires-3-dlc-uncancelled</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Matt Wales</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 14:45:25 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-age-of-empires-3-dlc-uncancelled</guid><category>Tantalus Media</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Strategy: Real-Time Strategy</category><category>PC</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Age of Empires III: Definitive Edition</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/aoe3-baltic-header.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/aoe3-baltic-header.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Here's something you don't hear very often, especially in a month as destructive as the one Xbox is having: Microsoft is seemingly uncancelling something; specifically its previously announced and then subsequently abandoned Age of Empires 3 DLC, which is now set to arrive this September.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-age-of-empires-3-dlc-uncancelled">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>A new Guild Wars 3 blog post spills the beans on the game's narrative focus, and perhaps even how magic will work in the upcoming MMORPG</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/guild-wars-3-narrative-magic-signets-spirits</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 14:41:05 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/guild-wars-3-narrative-magic-signets-spirits</guid><category>MMORPG</category><category>MMO</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Guild Wars 3</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/guild-wars-3-art.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/guild-wars-3-art.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>A new blog post has been released from ArenaNet, detailing some interesting story details for its upcoming MMORPG Guild Wars 3. However, present within the text might just be a hint to two into how magic will work in-game.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/guild-wars-3-narrative-magic-signets-spirits">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The big Final Fantasy 7 Revelation interview</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/the-big-final-fantasy-7-revelation-interview</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/the-big-final-fantasy-7-revelation-interview</guid><category>Square Enix</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><category>JRPG</category><category>Final Fantasy VII: Revelation</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/hamaguchi-ff7-r.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/hamaguchi-ff7-r.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>I think my favourite thing about the <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/final-fantasy-vii-remake">Final Fantasy 7 Remake</a> trilogy so far is the specific ways in which the developers at <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/square-enix">Square Enix</a> inject nostalgia. The games launched to date - Remake and Rebirth - manage to nod warmly towards aspects of the original RPG without it ever feeling trite. You can see it in so many aspects of the way the games are curated: the way certain musical sequences are teased as motifs, and then brought in, full-throated, for certain boss fights; the redesigns of (in)famous monsters, and how certain major enemies are deployed in slightly remixed ways for maximum effect; the reinterpretation and reimagination of dialogue to better fit the bigger, more complex world of 'the Planet' in 2020's version of the world compared to 1997's.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/the-big-final-fantasy-7-revelation-interview">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>PlayStation Network down, as tens of thousands of players queue to play Marvel Tokon Fighting Souls newly-launched beta</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/psn-network-down-login-failure</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 13:03:51 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/psn-network-down-login-failure</guid><category>PS5</category><category>PlayStation Network</category><category>Sony</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/marvel-tokon-iron-man.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/marvel-tokon-iron-man.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Reports of a PlayStation Network (PSN) outage are currently spiking, as many players are struggling to connect to online services.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/psn-network-down-login-failure">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>There's a Breakout movie on the way as Atari signs deal to bring Pong, Asteroids, and other classic games to the big screen</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/atari-movie-pong-breakout-asteroids-more</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Matt Wales</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:21:58 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/atari-movie-pong-breakout-asteroids-more</guid><category>Berzerk</category><category>PC</category><category>Asteroids</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Xbox 360</category><category>SEGA</category><category>Simulation</category><category>Namco</category><category>Missile Command</category><category>Glu Mobile</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Side view</category><category>Centipede</category><category>Sears</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Atari</category><category>bandai</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Taito Corporation</category><category>Pong</category><category>Arcade</category><category>Stainless Games</category><category>Playphone</category><category>Sports</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/breakout-cinema.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/breakout-cinema.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>In a surefire sign Hollywood has reached the desperation stage of its insatiable hunger for video game properties to swallow up and spit out in dubiously recognisable big-screen form, Atari has somewhat improbably announced a deal with Universal Pictures to produce ten movies based on classic retro games from its expansive backcatalogue, including Pong, Breakout, and more.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/atari-movie-pong-breakout-asteroids-more">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Kingdom Come Salvation may be the next Medieval RPG from Warhorse, and it could have some sort of multi-player functionality, too</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/kingdom-come-salvation-trademark-filing</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:20:54 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/kingdom-come-salvation-trademark-filing</guid><category>First person</category><category>Warhorse Studios</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Deep Silver</category><category>PC</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>PS4</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Kingdom Come: Deliverance II</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>RPG</category><category>Kingdom Come: Deliverance</category><category>Plaion</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Simulation</category><category>Mac</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kh-c-2-horse.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kh-c-2-horse.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>It looks like we've had our first hint as to what we can expect next from the Kingdom Come studio, Warhorse. We only heard back in May this year that <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/kingdom-come-deliverance-3-release-window">a third Kingdom Come RPG may be released sooner than we expected</a>, and it seems like the barely-announced title already has a name.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/kingdom-come-salvation-trademark-filing">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Ubisoft boss Yves Guillemot doesn't believe PlayStation ditching physical discs will "disturb" the industry much</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/ubisoft-ceo-playstation-disc-wont-disturb-industry</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:13:40 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/ubisoft-ceo-playstation-disc-wont-disturb-industry</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Physical Media</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Ubisoft Entertainment</category><category>Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced</category><category>Sony</category><category>Ubisoft Montreal</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/watch-dogs-legion_qQHG7BM.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/watch-dogs-legion_qQHG7BM.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Ubisoft CEO Yves Guillemot has chimed in on the debate surrounding Sony's planned shift away from physical disc production, stating he doesn't think it will "disturb" the industry too much.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/ubisoft-ceo-playstation-disc-wont-disturb-industry">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"We still value the culture of physical media" As PlayStation prepares for an all-digital future, Sega president comes out in support of discs</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-sega-ceo</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 10:18:17 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-sega-ceo</guid><category>PS3</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Sonic The Hedgehog</category><category>SEGA Mega Drive</category><category>PC</category><category>Platformer</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Sonic Team</category><category>SEGA Australia</category><category>Side view</category><category>SEGA</category><category>Xbox 360</category><category>Android</category><category>Nintendo Wii</category><category>iOS</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/custom-image-sega-ceo.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/custom-image-sega-ceo.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Sega is the latest publisher to make its views about physical media clear, in the wake of Sony's controversial decision to <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-ending-playstation-discs-physical-media-january-2028">kill off the manufacture and sale of discs by 2028</a>. The president of the Japanese publisher, Shuji Utsumi, noted that he believes physical media is still important, though digital distribution is "crucial", mostly thanks to the "steadily increasing" number of people playing on PC.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-sega-ceo">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>If PlayStation kills physical media, it should "get rid of the hardware" too, says the creator of popular RPG series Disgaea</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-hardware-disgaea-creator</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 09:07:36 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-hardware-disgaea-creator</guid><category>NIS America</category><category>RPG</category><category>Disgaea</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>PS4</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Demons' Night Fever</category><category>Strategy: Turn-Based Strategy</category><category>Third person</category><category>Arc System Works</category><category>JRPG</category><category>Nippon Ichi Software</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Niikawa-discs.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Niikawa-discs.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Since 1st July, when Sony <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-ending-playstation-discs-physical-media-january-2028">announced its intent to move away from the production and sale of physical media</a>, we've seen plenty of backlash from both consumers and those working within the video game industry. There's plenty of evidence of this, but the most vocal and visceral has come <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/marvels-wolverine-story-trailer-sony-disc-outrage">from comments on pretty much anything Sony has posted</a> online in the days since the announcement.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-physical-media-hardware-disgaea-creator">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Xbox rolls out ad-supported game streaming test for its insider programs, as hardware supply and affordability crisis rages on</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-game-advertising-insider-affordability</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 09:06:17 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-game-advertising-insider-affordability</guid><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Xbox One</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/halo-infinite-campaign-review-master-chief-makes-a-leap-of-faith-and-nails-the-landing-1638458496549.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/halo-infinite-campaign-review-master-chief-makes-a-leap-of-faith-and-nails-the-landing-1638458496549.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Xbox has announced a test for an ad-supporting streaming service for its Xbox Insider program. It will allow players to stream select games from their library for free for one-hour sessions, with advertisements playing before play sessions.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-game-advertising-insider-affordability">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced has already sold over 3.5 million copies, "exceeding annual expectations within its first 14 days"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-sales-exceed-annual-expectations</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 24 Jul 2026 08:46:13 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-sales-exceed-annual-expectations</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Ubisoft Entertainment</category><category>Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced</category><category>Ubisoft Montreal</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kenway-cash.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kenway-cash.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Assassin's Creed Black Flag is going from strength-to-strength for Ubisoft. After <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-resynced-2-million-sales">netting 2m sales</a> in its opening few days (and then <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-resynced-3-million-copies-one-week">ascending to 3m within a week</a>), Ubisoft has just announced that the game has sold through an impressive 3.5m units - meaning the remake has "exceeded annual expectations within its first 14 days", per <a href="https://staticctf.ubisoft.com/8aefmxkxpxwl/YIcpZgz0odIOM2V7Uz1ho/c6ee19fdfacb61d5483f0ca98d578ac7/Ubisoft_FY27_Q1_PR_English_vF.pdf">a new financial report</a> from the publisher.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-sales-exceed-annual-expectations">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>As layoff controversy continues, Rockstar union has 'more members than ever before', meaning it could force mandatory recognition</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/rockstar-developer-union-more-members-layoffs</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:37:40 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/rockstar-developer-union-more-members-layoffs</guid><category>Grand Theft Auto VI</category><category>Modern Day</category><category>Shooter: Third Person</category><category>First person</category><category>Take-Two Interactive</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Rockstar Games</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Third person</category><category>Full product</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Racing</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/grand-theft-auto-6-character-4k-wallpaper-uhdpaper.com-269%401%40n.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/grand-theft-auto-6-character-4k-wallpaper-uhdpaper.com-269%401%40n.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The Rockstar Game Workers Union (RGWU), which was formed earlier this year in response to the <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/former-rockstar-games-staff-were-fired-for-sharing-internal-company-messages-on-an-employee-and-union-only-discord-server-new-report-suggests">Grand Theft Auto 6 developer's massively controversial job cuts</a>, now has "more members than it ever had before".</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/rockstar-developer-union-more-members-layoffs">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Former Disney CEO Michael Eisner can't remember why he green-lit Kingdom Hearts</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/former-disney-ceo-cant-remember-why-kingdom-hearts</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 16:28:20 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/former-disney-ceo-cant-remember-why-kingdom-hearts</guid><category>Square Enix</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Sony Computer Entertainment Europe</category><category>Third person</category><category>Disney Interactive Studios</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Sony Computer Entertainment</category><category>PS2</category><category>RPG</category><category>Kingdom Hearts</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/KINGDOM-HEARTS-III-%E2%80%93-Opening-Movie-Trailer-1-23-screenshot.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/KINGDOM-HEARTS-III-%E2%80%93-Opening-Movie-Trailer-1-23-screenshot.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/kingdom-hearts">Kingdom Hearts</a> might be beloved by millions of players around the world, but it apparently didn't have a lasting impact on arguably one of the most important people involved in its creation: former Walt Disney CEO Michael Eisner has admitted he can't remember why he approved the pitch for <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/square-enix">Square Enix</a>'s legendary video game series.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/former-disney-ceo-cant-remember-why-kingdom-hearts">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Steam's latest update finally brings order to the chaos of your wishlist, and might even nudge people into buying you some new games</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/steam-wishlists-gifting-big-updates</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:32:45 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/steam-wishlists-gifting-big-updates</guid><category>Valve</category><category>PC</category><category>Steam</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/steam_share_image.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/steam_share_image.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>If you're among the millions whose Steam wishlists have been accumulating games for years, and you're too scared to venture in, Valve's latest Steam update should help.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/steam-wishlists-gifting-big-updates">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Halo: Campaign Evolved review</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/halo-campaign-evolved-review</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/halo-campaign-evolved-review</guid><category>First person</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Halo Studios</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Halo: Campaign Evolved</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>FPS</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/halo-campaign-evolved_MmWCvSL.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/halo-campaign-evolved_MmWCvSL.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>When Master Chief first sets foot on the unknown ringworld known as Halo, he is fighting for his life. Harried and ambushed by countless enemy ships, Chief's commanding officer scuttles their intergalactic craft upon the ringworld - assuming the human troops will fare better on this structure than face a cold, indifferent death in the vacuum of space. But once they set foot upon Halo, they realise all is not what it seems; here, they are trespassing on the work of a culture that has come before. They are treading on the face of a masterpiece. Interfering with greatness. I can't help but see the parallels to Halo Studios and Bungie.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/halo-campaign-evolved-review">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>EU approves Saudi Arabia's $55bn acquisition of EA, clearing path for largest private leveraged buyout of all time</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/saudi-arabian-pif-aquisition-electronic-arts-approved-european-union</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 14:44:21 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/saudi-arabian-pif-aquisition-electronic-arts-approved-european-union</guid><category>EA</category><category>Saudi Arabia</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/mass-effect-shepard-sad.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/mass-effect-shepard-sad.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The European Union has approved the controversial <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/ea-privately-acquired-in-55bn-deal-by-group-of-investors-including-saudi-arabias-investment-fund-and-donald-trumps-son-in-law">$55bn acquisition of Electronic Arts by Saudi Arabia's Public Investment Fund</a> (PIF), private equity company Silver Lake, and investment company Affinity Partners.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/saudi-arabian-pif-aquisition-electronic-arts-approved-european-union">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Resident Evil movie gets another spooky trailer, and features a fun game reference for keen-eyed fans</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/resident-evil-movie-new-trailer-july-hosptial</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:52:45 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/resident-evil-movie-new-trailer-july-hosptial</guid><category>Columbia Pictures</category><category>Resident Evil</category><category>Blockbuster</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/a-scared-man-shines-a-light-from-(I-think)-his-phone-is-Resident-Evil-movie-trailer.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/a-scared-man-shines-a-light-from-(I-think)-his-phone-is-Resident-Evil-movie-trailer.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>A new trailer for the upcoming Resident Evil movie has been released, introducing the call-to-action for our protagonist's journey into the dark and spooky world of bio terror. It also features a nice little easter egg for keen-eyed fans of the games.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/resident-evil-movie-new-trailer-july-hosptial">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Former PlayStation boss Shawn Layden wants to save games by bringing back double-A - and he has a plan</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/former-playstation-boss-shawn-layden-bringing-double-a-back</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:35:11 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/former-playstation-boss-shawn-layden-bringing-double-a-back</guid><category>Modern Day</category><category>Warhammer 40.000: Space Marine 2</category><category>Neowiz</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Focus Home Interactive</category><category>PC</category><category>Lies of P</category><category>RPG</category><category>Take-Two Interactive</category><category>Grand Theft Auto VI</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Rockstar Games</category><category>Focus Entertainment</category><category>Third person</category><category>Full product</category><category>RoboCop: Rogue City</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Open World</category><category>First person</category><category>Teyon</category><category>Nacon</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Mac</category><category>Shooter: Third Person</category><category>Saber Interactive</category><category>PS4</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Racing</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/robocop-layden.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/robocop-layden.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>He's been saying it for years: blockbuster game development is unsustainable today, and given that Shawn Layden used to lead PlayStation's entire roster of first-party studios, he likely knows a fair bit about the issue. "Every generation it costs twice as much to build a game," <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/there-comes-a-time-when-we-all-declare-the-war-is-over-former-playstation-studios-boss-shawn-layden-on-the-future-of-video-game-consoles">he told Tom Phillips more recently.</a></p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/former-playstation-boss-shawn-layden-bringing-double-a-back">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Call of Duty: Black Ops 7 will very soon offer three different matchmaking systems, and you'd be right to be confused</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-classic-matchmaking-black-ops-1-2</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 13:20:17 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-classic-matchmaking-black-ops-1-2</guid><category>Modern Day</category><category>PC</category><category>Military</category><category>Square Enix</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Treyarch</category><category>PS5</category><category>Call of Duty: Black Ops 7</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Activision</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Realism</category><category>Raven Software</category><category>Infinity Ward</category><category>FPS</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>PS4</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4 (2026)</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/black-ops-7-season-5-screen-3.jpeg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/black-ops-7-season-5-screen-3.jpeg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Call of Duty has brought matchmaking back into the conversation. Activision has announced that <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/call-of-duty-black-ops-7">Black Ops 7</a> is introducing a new matchmaking system, available to players today with the launch of Season 5.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-black-ops-7-classic-matchmaking-black-ops-1-2">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"The smallest severance pay possible" - Bethesda union vows to fight as studio employees reel from "bare minimum" payout following mass Xbox layoffs</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/bethesda-montreal-smallest-severance-possible</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:27:59 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/bethesda-montreal-smallest-severance-possible</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>Microsoft</category><category>RPG</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><category>Layoffs</category><category>PS5</category><category>The Elder Scrolls VI</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bethesda Game Studios</category><category>Open World</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Starfield</category><category>FPS</category><category>union</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Science Fiction</category><category>Fallout 5</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Fallout-4-update_sAo2i7i.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Fallout-4-update_sAo2i7i.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-xbox-layoffs-2026-double-fine-compulsion-ninja-theory">Following Xbox mass layoffs earlier this month</a>, employees at Bethesda's Montr&eacute;al studio have reportedly been told they'll receive the "smallest" severance pay legally possible.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/bethesda-montreal-smallest-severance-possible">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>After its Baldur's Gate 3-era splurge, Hasbro is scaling back its gaming ambitions following $56m loss, but Warlock and Mass Effect-like Exodus are safe</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/hasbro-56-million-usd-write-down-exodus-warlock-fate</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 12:00:35 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/hasbro-56-million-usd-write-down-exodus-warlock-fate</guid><category>Invoke Studios</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Hasbro</category><category>PS5</category><category>Archetype Entertainment</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>RPG: Action</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Warlock (2027)</category><category>Warlock: Dungeons and Dragons</category><category>Wizards of the Coast</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><category>Exodus (2027)</category><category>Dungeons &amp; Dragons</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/exodus-2.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/exodus-2.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Hasbro, the parent company of Dungeons and Dragons owner Wizards of the Coast, is seemingly scaling back its video game ambitions. The company, which had initiated a plan in 2022 to become a major publisher, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/dungeons-dragons-owner-wizards-of-the-coast-reportedly-cancels-at-least-five-unannounced-video-games">has already cancelled several of its projects</a> and laid off many of their developers.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/hasbro-56-million-usd-write-down-exodus-warlock-fate">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Xbox version of Avatar Legends: The Fighting Game delayed by over a month, less than 24 hours before launch</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/avatar-legends-fighting-game-xbox-delay-switch-version</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 08:56:39 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/avatar-legends-fighting-game-xbox-delay-switch-version</guid><category>Avatar Legends: The Fighting Game</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>Third person</category><category>PM Studios</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Side view</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Fighting</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/avatar-legends-korra.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/avatar-legends-korra.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Less than 24 hours before its intended release date, the developers behind the Avatar Legends: The Fighting Game <a href="https://x.com/avatar_fighters/status/2080094735314677888">have announced</a> some serious disruptions to the launch on Xbox and Nintendo Switch.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/avatar-legends-fighting-game-xbox-delay-switch-version">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Stalker 2 developer refutes claims by studio founder that Xbox paid more than game's development cost to make it exclusive</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/stalker-2-xbox-timed-exclusivity-claim-refuted</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 23 Jul 2026 08:19:11 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/stalker-2-xbox-timed-exclusivity-claim-refuted</guid><category>First person</category><category>GSC Game World</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Single Player</category><category>S.T.A.L.K.E.R. 2: Heart of Chornobyl</category><category>Microsoft</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ss_bb0d9a5b981ada1e0045cc49327e2cc26566766f.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ss_bb0d9a5b981ada1e0045cc49327e2cc26566766f.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Earlier this week, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/gsc-game-world">GSC Game World</a> studio founder Sergiy Grygorovych made a bombshell revelation about the development of <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/stalker-2-heart-of-chornobyl-review">Stalker 2: Heart of Chornobyl</a>. Grygorovych said in an interview with YouTuber <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@oldboiua">OLDboi</a> that Microsoft paid a significant sum to keep the then-upcoming open-world shooter a timed Xbox exclusive.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/stalker-2-xbox-timed-exclusivity-claim-refuted">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Following layoffs and muddy strategy shifts, Xbox announces Backward Compatibility on PC program, with Blinx and Conker leading the first wave</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-backward-compatibility-on-pc-announced</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 15:55:20 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-backward-compatibility-on-pc-announced</guid><category>Microsoft Studios</category><category>Game Pass</category><category>Artoon</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Xbox</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Rare</category><category>Conker: Live and Reloaded</category><category>PC</category><category>Platformer</category><category>Blinx: The Time Sweeper</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Third person</category><category>Microsoft</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Blinx-The-Time-Sweeper.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Blinx-The-Time-Sweeper.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>As Microsoft tries to downplay the effects on its gaming business of <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-xbox-layoffs-2026-double-fine-compulsion-ninja-theory">cutting 3,200 jobs and four studios</a>, Xbox is rethinking its whole strategy even if the more recent comments from inside the house <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-leadership-on-future-exclusives">still sound confused at best</a>. Don't worry though; old Xbox games are coming to PC.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-backward-compatibility-on-pc-announced">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Splatoon Raiders developers reveal it originally was "like a base defence game" before evolving into a faster spin-off "with a strong sense of action"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/splatoon-raiders-original-idea</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:55:16 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/splatoon-raiders-original-idea</guid><category>Nintendo</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Splatoon Raiders</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/NSwitch2_SplatoonRaiders_Mechanic_02.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/NSwitch2_SplatoonRaiders_Mechanic_02.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/splatoon-raiders">Splatoon Raiders</a> will attempt to make a splash tomorrow, 23rd July, and Nintendo is celebrating its launch on <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/platforms/switch-2">Switch 2</a> with a surprisingly in-depth chat with four key Nintendo EPD developers.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/splatoon-raiders-original-idea">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Of all the platforms, Xbox is the only one to have just grown year-on-year - but there's a big catch</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/circana-june-2026-game-hardware-xbox-growth-software-sales</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 14:03:51 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/circana-june-2026-game-hardware-xbox-growth-software-sales</guid><category>Indie</category><category>Party</category><category>First person</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Circana</category><category>Stealth</category><category>Meccha Chameleon</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Star Fox (2026)</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/xbox_hPBubF0.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/xbox_hPBubF0.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Market analysis firm Circana has published the latest edition of its monthly report, which tracks spending across game hardware and software in the US. June's edition is another bleak one, with a near-universal decline.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/circana-june-2026-game-hardware-xbox-growth-software-sales">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Palworld has sold over 30m copies already, with Steam unsurprisingly emerging as the most popular platform</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-30-million-sales</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 13:55:33 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-30-million-sales</guid><category>Indie</category><category>Pocketpair</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>RPG</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Palworld</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>PS4</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><category>Mac</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Palworld-female-character.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Palworld-female-character.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-player-count-launch-weekend">Palworld's 1.0 release</a> has been massive so far, with the game <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-almost-hits-1-million-concurrents-again">hitting its biggest concurrent player peaks since the 2024 early access launch</a> for the past two weeks. Unsurprisingly, that has also translated into a boost to premium unit sales.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-30-million-sales">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Sony's decision to kill off PlayStation discs could destroy the $7.2bn used game market, according to analysts</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/used-video-game-market-at-risk-sony-killing-playstation-discs</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 12:19:08 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/used-video-game-market-at-risk-sony-killing-playstation-discs</guid><category>PS6</category><category>PS5</category><category>eBay</category><category>PS4</category><category>Cex Ltd</category><category>Microsoft</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>used game market</category><category>Sony Interactive Entertainment</category><category>GameStop</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/discs-playstation.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/discs-playstation.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The second-hand video game market stands in jeopardy in the wake of <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-ending-playstation-discs-physical-media-january-2028">Sony's decision to end the manufacturing of PlayStation discs by January 2028</a>. The market, which analysts estimate is worth $7.2bn globally, could be destroyed as a result of Sony's controversial move.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/used-video-game-market-at-risk-sony-killing-playstation-discs">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Here's your next batch of Xbox Game Pass games for July</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-game-pass-july-wave-2</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 11:30:11 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-game-pass-july-wave-2</guid><category>Halo Studios</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>RPG</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Game Freak</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Game Pass</category><category>First person</category><category>Halo: Campaign Evolved</category><category>Nacon</category><category>Shooter</category><category>FPS</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Hell is Us</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Beast of Reincarnation</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Halo-CE_key-art_Xbox-logo_custom.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Halo-CE_key-art_Xbox-logo_custom.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Xbox <a href="https://news.xbox.com/en-us/2026/07/21/xbox-game-pass-july-2026-wave-2/">has revealed</a> the next batch of games coming to its Xbox Game Pass subscription service during the remainder of July and in early August, with <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/halo-campaign-evolved">Halo: Campaign Evolved</a> and <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/hell-is-us">Hell Is Us</a> spearheading the selection.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-game-pass-july-wave-2">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Blizzard's calling time on Overwatch's hero customising Stadium mode, and I may well be the only person that's sad about that</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/overwatch-stadium-support-ending</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:58:18 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/overwatch-stadium-support-ending</guid><category>First person</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>PS4</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Third person</category><category>Blizzard Entertainment</category><category>Activision Blizzard</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Overwatch (2026)</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/overwatch-stadium-sad.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/overwatch-stadium-sad.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Live service games face an interesting conundrum, I think: how do you keep offering the core experience of a game while also periodically reinventing it, and varying it, in such a way that will make it feel new? <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/overwatch">Overwatch</a> is a game facing such a conundrum, and Blizzard has tried all kinds of different things to mix it up: switching to five-person teams from six, developing a PvE mode that never materialised, and for the past year or so, offering a MOBA-like mode called Stadium. But now Stadium has been earmarked for the scrapheap.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/overwatch-stadium-support-ending">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Asha Sharma-appointed Xbox VP of engineering leaves just three months after moving over from Microsoft's CoreAI team</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-vp-engineering-leaves-after-three-months</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 10:36:09 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-vp-engineering-leaves-after-three-months</guid><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Xbox One</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/xbox-logo_OJRhRlL.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/xbox-logo_OJRhRlL.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>When Microsoft <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/today-marks-an-exciting-new-chapter-xbox-boss-phil-spencer-retiring-amid-major-leadership-shakeup-that-sees-microsofts-coreai-president-taking-over-roll">assigned Asha Sharma as the new leader of the Xbox division in February</a>, replacing the <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/personas/phil-spencer">Phil Spencer</a> regime, the executive brought along some of her former colleagues with her. Now, one of those recent hires is leaving.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-vp-engineering-leaves-after-three-months">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Reddit is forcing Google AI into hallucinating The Duskbloods characters before FromSoftware's Switch 2 exclusive is even out</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/the-duskbloods-google-ai-hallucinations</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 09:28:39 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/the-duskbloods-google-ai-hallucinations</guid><category>Nintendo</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>FromSoftware</category><category>Third person</category><category>The Duskbloods</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/duskbloods-gemini.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/duskbloods-gemini.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/the-duskbloods">The Duskbloods</a>' first playtest - which will likely mark the first time anyone outside FromSoftware and Nintendo has played the <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/platforms/switch-2">Switch 2</a> exclusive - <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/the-duskbloods-closed-playtest-dates">is coming next month</a>, yet Google's AI search believes the subreddit <a href="https://www.reddit.com/r/TheDuskbloods/">r/TheDuskbloods</a> already has official information.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/the-duskbloods-google-ai-hallucinations">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The Incident at Galley House review</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/the-incident-at-galley-house-review</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Matt Wales</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/the-incident-at-galley-house-review</guid><category>Indie</category><category>Story Rich</category><category>Puzzle</category><category>PC</category><category>Text</category><category>The Incident at Galley House</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Interactive Drama</category><category>Evil Trout</category><category>Mac</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/galley-house-header-3.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/galley-house-header-3.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>There's a machine in The Incident at Galley House you'll spend an awful lot of time with, and it's a wonderfully tactile thing. It's part mixing desk, part paranormal enigma, part over-engineered Guess Who game, and full of clicky dials, chunky buttons, and a big old whooshy lever you're forever manipulating. And if your deductive instincts are good enough, it whirs into crackling life like a haunted slot machine, rigged to deliver strange psychic visions.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/the-incident-at-galley-house-review">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Mortal Shell 2 sells out of physical Revered Edition PS5 pre-orders as players rush to buy the highly-anticipated game on disc</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/mortal-shell-2-revered-edition-ps5-disc-sold-out</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Wed, 22 Jul 2026 08:36:07 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/mortal-shell-2-revered-edition-ps5-disc-sold-out</guid><category>Cold Symmetry</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Playstack</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Mortal Shell II</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/mortal-shell-2-gameplay-screen-1.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/mortal-shell-2-gameplay-screen-1.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>With a little under one month left until the launch of Soulslike Mortal Shell 2, one of the game's physical versions can no longer be pre-ordered. Stock of the &pound;55 ($70) PlayStation 5 Revered Edition is completely depleted, publisher Playstack announced.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/mortal-shell-2-revered-edition-ps5-disc-sold-out">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Darkest Dungeon is getting its first dollop of DLC in several years, as the gloomy old RPG celebrates its 10th birthday</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/darkest-dungeon-the-fires-edge-dlc-reveal</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 16:13:15 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/darkest-dungeon-the-fires-edge-dlc-reveal</guid><category>Darkest Dungeon</category><category>Indie</category><category>iOS</category><category>Red Hook Studios</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>PS4</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Strategy: Turn-Based Strategy</category><category>Side view</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>RPG</category><category>PlayStation Vita</category><category>Mac</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Darkest-Dungeon-2---The-Fire's-Edge.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Darkest-Dungeon-2---The-Fire's-Edge.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/darkest-dungeon-2">Darkest Dungeon 2</a> landed well enough and received <a href="https://www.metacritic.com/game/darkest-dungeon-ii/">generally positive reviews</a>, but it's never been universally accepted in the same way the original game was, as <a href="https://store.steampowered.com/app/1940340/Darkest_Dungeon_II/">Steam user reviews of Darkest Dungeon 2</a> highlight. Now, developer Red Hook Studios is surprising fans with a return to the original game.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/darkest-dungeon-the-fires-edge-dlc-reveal">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Jagex wants classic British point-and-click MMO RuneScape to be bigger than World of Warcraft</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/jagex-runescape-bigger-than-world-of-warcraft</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 16:09:30 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/jagex-runescape-bigger-than-world-of-warcraft</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>RPG</category><category>Android</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Text</category><category>Third person</category><category>Fantasy</category><category>Single Player</category><category>RuneScape: Dragonwilds</category><category>Survival &amp; Crafting</category><category>Open World</category><category>iOS</category><category>Old School RuneScape</category><category>Exploration</category><category>RPG: Action</category><category>RuneScape</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Point and Click</category><category>Mac</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Jagex Games Studio</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/RuneScape_Dragonwilds_Armor_1.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/RuneScape_Dragonwilds_Armor_1.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Jagex CEO Jon Bellamy has shared his lofty aspiration for <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/runescape">RuneScape</a> to be the biggest MMO in the world in the next five years. That, for those unaware, would mean toppling World of Warcraft from the top spot.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/jagex-runescape-bigger-than-world-of-warcraft">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The FBI has arrested a 21-year-old alleged to have stolen $220,000 through Steam using malware-ridden games</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/fbi-arrest-21-year-old-stolen-crypto-currency</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 15:50:54 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/fbi-arrest-21-year-old-stolen-crypto-currency</guid><category>iOS</category><category>First person</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Mac</category><category>Puzzle</category><category>PC</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Angry Bugs</category><category>Activision</category><category>Hacker</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/sombra-hacking-overwatch.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/sombra-hacking-overwatch.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The FBI has arrested a 21-year-old Florida man alleged to have stolen roughly $220,000 of crypto currency using malware installed alongside games. And while the PC platform used to nab this catch isn't explicitly specified, the infested games listed by the FBI were present on Steam until recently.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/fbi-arrest-21-year-old-stolen-crypto-currency">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Slay the Spire 2 developer shows artwork and concepts for Doormaker boss replacement Aeonglass</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/slay-the-spire-2-aeonglass-design-process</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 15:32:05 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/slay-the-spire-2-aeonglass-design-process</guid><category>Indie</category><category>PC</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Side view</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Slay the Spire 2</category><category>Card Games</category><category>Mac</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Slay-the-Spire-2-Aeonglass-designs.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Slay-the-Spire-2-Aeonglass-designs.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Last month, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/slay-the-spire">Slay the Spire</a> 2's <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/slay-the-spire-2-beta-patch-cuts-act-3-boss-doormaker-introduces-bestiary">Act 3 boss Doormaker</a> - the third in a series of late-game reworks - was removed and replaced by Aeonglass. Now, developer Mega Crit has revealed how its fun visual design came to be.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/slay-the-spire-2-aeonglass-design-process">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Nintendo has no obligation to pass tariff refunds onto customers, the company says, because Switch buyers received "what they bargained and paid for"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/nintendo-us-tariffs-no-switch-refunds-class-action-lawsuit</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:09:55 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/nintendo-us-tariffs-no-switch-refunds-class-action-lawsuit</guid><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/An-original-Switch-console-against-an-American-flag-background.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/An-original-Switch-console-against-an-American-flag-background.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Nintendo has said it does not owe people who bought its products at higher prices any rebates, after the company raised prices in response to inflated US tariffs. The Japanese gaming giant is seeking the dismissal of a class-action lawsuit that argues this exact case: that consumers deserve a portion of the refund Nintendo could receive from the US government.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/nintendo-us-tariffs-no-switch-refunds-class-action-lawsuit">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>What does the next 10 years hold for Pokémon Go? More mechanics, better gyms, and "multi-generational play"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/pokemon-go-next-10-years-gym-multi-generation-more-mechanics</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 14:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/pokemon-go-next-10-years-gym-multi-generation-more-mechanics</guid><category>Social</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>RPG</category><category>Simulation</category><category>Android</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>The Pokémon Company International</category><category>Side view</category><category>Free-2-Play</category><category>Open World</category><category>iOS</category><category>First person</category><category>Pokémon Go</category><category>Niantic</category><category>Scopely Explore</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Family-friendly</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>Anime</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/pogo-10-years.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/pogo-10-years.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/pokemon-go">Pok&eacute;mon Go</a> is celebrating its 10th anniversary this year. The game, which famously uses GPS and augmented reality to let you discover, catch, and battle virtual monsters in real-world locations, took the world by storm in 2016. Blurring the line between mainstream and niche gaming interest, Pok&eacute;mon Go has retained a lot of popularity in the interceding 10 years since it launched, with <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/pokemon-go-10th-anniversary-mewtwo-times-square">a recent New York event even managing to take over Times Square</a> - a fate promised in the game's initial launch trailer a whole decade ago.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/pokemon-go-next-10-years-gym-multi-generation-more-mechanics">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Xbox Game Pass was a good idea in theory, former Forza Horizon 5 director says, but "the reality is not enough people have subscribed"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/forza-horizon-5-director-comments-xbox-game-pass</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 13:59:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/forza-horizon-5-director-comments-xbox-game-pass</guid><category>First person</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Playground Games</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Racing</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Forza Horizon 5</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ss_1da0673f82eccc3c9d222237dec40e36bf10eef3.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ss_1da0673f82eccc3c9d222237dec40e36bf10eef3.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Mike Brown, ex-director on <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/forza-horizon-5">Forza Horizon 5</a> at Playground Games, has commented on Xbox's current problems and <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-game-pass-games-list-this-month-price-6400">Game Pass</a>' impact on the brand's overarching strategy in recent years.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/forza-horizon-5-director-comments-xbox-game-pass">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Splatoon Raiders review</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/splatoon-raiders-review</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Christian Donlan</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 13:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/splatoon-raiders-review</guid><category>Nintendo</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Splatoon Raiders</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/splatoon-raiders-review-header.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/splatoon-raiders-review-header.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>This series offshoot is a hectic, often overwhelming delight.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/splatoon-raiders-review">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Once you see it, you can't unsee it: Hilarity ensues as new DC Comics fighting game is named DCKO</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/warner-bros-dcko-dc-fighting-game-mobile-announced</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:27:50 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/warner-bros-dcko-dc-fighting-game-mobile-announced</guid><category>Fighting</category><category>DCKO</category><category>Android</category><category>iOS</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/dcko-constantine.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/dcko-constantine.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>A new fighting game has been announced! Making use of the rich DC universe, this upcoming release brings free-to-play 2v2 brawling to mobile. Its name? Um, DCKO.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/warner-bros-dcko-dc-fighting-game-mobile-announced">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic remake might be re-revealed this year, a new report suggests</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/star-wars-kotor-remake-reveal-rumours</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 12:22:49 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/star-wars-kotor-remake-reveal-rumours</guid><category>Aspyr</category><category>PS5</category><category>Saber Interactive</category><category>PC</category><category>Lucasfilm Games</category><category>RPG</category><category>Embracer Group</category><category>Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic Remake</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kotor_kQM9BLI.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kotor_kQM9BLI.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The on-again, off-again <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/star-wars-knights-of-the-old-republic-remake">Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic remake</a> - which was first announced in late 2021 before <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/kotor-remake-alive-and-well-says-saber-interactive-ceo">changing studios</a> - may be re-revealed as soon as this year.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/star-wars-kotor-remake-reveal-rumours">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon Wildlands appears to be getting a PS5 and Xbox Series X/S Definitive Edition, but is it a remaster or a bog standard re-release?</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/ghost-recon-wildlands-definitive-edition-leak</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 11:58:54 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/ghost-recon-wildlands-definitive-edition-leak</guid><category>Ubisoft Paris</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon: Breakpoint</category><category>PC</category><category>RPG</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon: Wildlands</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Massive Entertainment</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>PS4</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Stadia</category><category>Ubisoft Entertainment</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Tom Clancy's The Division</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ghost-recon-wildlands-latest-update-drops-cheeky-nod-to-rainbox-sixs-cancelled-patriots-game-1532590213465.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ghost-recon-wildlands-latest-update-drops-cheeky-nod-to-rainbox-sixs-cancelled-patriots-game-1532590213465.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>If you've been itching to replay <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/tom-clancys-ghost-recon">Tom Clancy's Ghost Recon</a> Wildlands, for some reason, you may soon have a reason to. The open-world co-op shooter will be 10 years old next March and it looks like Ubisoft is celebrating the anniversary early.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/ghost-recon-wildlands-definitive-edition-leak">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>007 First Light's secret best character was a perfect way for IO Interactive to celebrate British writing and "restrained emotion"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/007-first-light-britishness-john-greenway</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 11:09:04 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/007-first-light-britishness-john-greenway</guid><category>IO Interactive</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>007 First Light</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/greenway-007-first-light.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/greenway-007-first-light.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/io-interactive">IO Interactive</a> has shared more development insight about arguably the stand-out character in 007 First Light: James Bond's mentor figure, John Greenway. This is the character played brilliantly by Walking Dead and Line of Duty actor Lennie James - a character as welcoming as a locked door when Bond initially joins the resurrected double-O secret agent training programme at the beginning of the game, but who gradually opens up.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/007-first-light-britishness-john-greenway">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The next major moment for Marathon arrives today with a new update and the debut of its PvE mode, Vault Breaker</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/marathon-vault-breaker-pve-mode-details-gameplay</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 10:45:16 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/marathon-vault-breaker-pve-mode-details-gameplay</guid><category>iOS</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bungie</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Marathon</category><category>Mac</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/marathon-shells-3.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/marathon-shells-3.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Bungie has shown off Vault Breaker in a new gameplay trailer. This is Marathon's experimental, time-limited PvE mode, which arrives today in Season 2's mid-season update. Vault Breaker is a roguelite mode that exists separately from the normal modes. In other words, it's not simply a PvE toggle you can turn on across the game.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/marathon-vault-breaker-pve-mode-details-gameplay">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Xbox admits its game exclusivity strategy isn't "obvious", but insists Gears of War and Clockwork Revolution won't be the only non-PlayStation games</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-leadership-on-future-exclusives</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 10:35:13 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-leadership-on-future-exclusives</guid><category>First person</category><category>RPG</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Clockwork Revolution</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Gears of War: E-day</category><category>The Coalition</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>inXile Entertainment</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Screenshot-from-Gears-of-War-E-Day.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Screenshot-from-Gears-of-War-E-Day.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Another day, another update on what's happening over at Xbox after <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/everything-announced-microsofts-xbox-games-showcase">last month's showcase</a> and <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-xbox-layoffs-2026-double-fine-compulsion-ninja-theory">the subsequent cuts of 3,200 jobs and studio divestments</a>. The matter at hand today: console exclusives, and <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-console-exclusive-strategy-clockwork-revolution-gears-of-war-e-day">based on past comments by Xbox</a>, we don't really know what to expect or what's going on.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-leadership-on-future-exclusives">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>What sense can we make of the madness at id Software?</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/what-sense-to-make-from-id-software-layoffs-microsoft-xbox</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rick Lane</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 09:39:30 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/what-sense-to-make-from-id-software-layoffs-microsoft-xbox</guid><category>Doom (2016)</category><category>Horror</category><category>Doom Eternal</category><category>PC</category><category>Microsoft</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><category>PS5</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>Doom: The Dark Ages</category><category>Single Player</category><category>id Software</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>FPS</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>PS4</category><category>Stadia</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/id-software-staff-photo.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/id-software-staff-photo.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>In a grim week for the games industry where Microsoft laid off 1,600 people (with 1,600 further job cuts hanging over the heads of Xbox employees) one decision stood out as especially egregious. Id Software, developer of Doom and Quake, was forced to lay off 136 people &ndash; more than half of its workforce.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/what-sense-to-make-from-id-software-layoffs-microsoft-xbox">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Despite outrage at Sony's shift towards a discless future, only seven PlayStation games have managed more than 100,000 physical sales in the US this year</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-disc-sales--outrage-circana</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 08:54:54 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-disc-sales--outrage-circana</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Insomniac Games</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Marvel's Wolverine</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/discs-playstation.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/discs-playstation.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Sony's planned shift away from producing physical discs for PlayStation might be unpopular, but new sales data has highlighted the stark business reality behind it.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/playstation-disc-sales--outrage-circana">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Modern Warfare 4 open and closed beta dates announced, including for Switch 2, alongside the return of Call of Duty: Next</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-beta-dates-switch-2-next</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Tue, 21 Jul 2026 08:37:17 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-beta-dates-switch-2-next</guid><category>Modern Day</category><category>Call of Duty: Next</category><category>First person</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Realism</category><category>PC</category><category>Infinity Ward</category><category>Single Player</category><category>FPS</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Military</category><category>Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4 (2026)</category><category>Activision</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/modern-warfare-4-multiplayer-beta-screen-1.jpeg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/modern-warfare-4-multiplayer-beta-screen-1.jpeg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Activision has finally revealed some worthwhile new details about what the next few months will look like in the lead-up to the release of Modern Warfare 4. The company officially announced the return of Call of Duty: Next, the event that has, for the last several years, served as the home for the debut of multiplayer gameplay.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-beta-dates-switch-2-next">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Battlefield 6's newest and largest map is good, but I worry it will end up being nothing more than a curiosity</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-season-4-tsuru-reef-preview</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 16:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-season-4-tsuru-reef-preview</guid><category>PS3</category><category>Battlefield 4</category><category>PC</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Xbox 360</category><category>Battlefield 6</category><category>Simulation</category><category>EA DICE</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>PS4</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Electronic Arts</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/battlefield-6-season-4-gameplay-screen-3.jpeg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/battlefield-6-season-4-gameplay-screen-3.jpeg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>There's been one thought I haven't been able to shake during my time with <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/battlefield-2025">Battlefield 6</a>'s upcoming Tsuru Reef map - the game's biggest yet, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-top-gun-collaboration-season-4-carrier-strike">which arrives tomorrow with Season 4</a>. Tsuru Reef is the item on a restaurant's menu that you tell yourself you'll try one day, yet you keep ordering the usual every time you visit. But just as that restaurant's menu is richer for having this delectable curiosity, Tsuru Reef is an asset to BF6's map line-up - even if I fear it's only going to get played occasionally.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-season-4-tsuru-reef-preview">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>After Doom director Hugo Martin denied reports that id Software had been gutted, "current and former employees" are disagreeing with his optimism</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/id-software-developers-comments-hugo-martin-layoffs</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:47:48 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/id-software-developers-comments-hugo-martin-layoffs</guid><category>Doom (2016)</category><category>Horror</category><category>Doom Eternal</category><category>PC</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><category>PS5</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>Doom: The Dark Ages</category><category>Single Player</category><category>id Software</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>FPS</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>PS4</category><category>Stadia</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/doom_image.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/doom_image.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>It's been two weeks since <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-xbox-layoffs-2026-double-fine-compulsion-ninja-theory">Microsoft announced 3,200 layoffs and sweeping cuts hit the Xbox division</a>. Not even well-established institutions like Doom and Quake studio id Software were safe - <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/xbox-layoffs-july-2026-id-software">with the first reports painting a very bleak picture</a> - yet Hugo Martin, director on the latest Doom entries, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/id-software-xbox-cuts-doom">pushed back</a> against claims the iconic FPS developer had been turned into <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/doom-quake-studio-id-software-gutted-xbox-cuts-game-ideas">little more than a support studio</a>. A few days later, "current and former employees" are saying they aren't as optimistic as Martin.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/id-software-developers-comments-hugo-martin-layoffs">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>A religious war is raging right now, as people are dressing in robes and rushing into danger in Old School RuneScape</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/religious-war-old-school-runescape</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:25:55 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/religious-war-old-school-runescape</guid><category>Old School RuneScape</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Mac</category><category>Text</category><category>PC</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Jagex Games Studio</category><category>RPG</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Android</category><category>iOS</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/osrs-monk-raid.jpeg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/osrs-monk-raid.jpeg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Do you ever get a hankering to bust out the fancy robes, grab a staff, and venture out into the wild with a gaggle of your friends? Well, good news! Religious war is back in a big way, in Old School <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/runescape">RuneScape</a>.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/religious-war-old-school-runescape">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Ever wanted to play The Elder Scrolls: Morrowind on a dual-screen handheld? Well, now you can - if you don't mind putting in some legwork</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/morrowind-ds-mod</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 15:02:41 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/morrowind-ds-mod</guid><category>First person</category><category>The Elder Scrolls III: Morrowind</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bethesda Game Studios</category><category>Ubisoft</category><category>ZeniMax Media</category><category>RPG</category><category>Xbox</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/morrowind_i0an2c5.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/morrowind_i0an2c5.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/the-elder-scrolls-6">The Elder Scrolls 6</a> isn't anywhere near done, and you might be getting tired of replaying <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/the-elder-scrolls-v-skyrim">Skyrim</a> and <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/the-elder-scrolls-4-oblivion-remake">Oblivion</a> over and over again across several platforms. But don't worry, as the Elder Scrolls community has now cracked a surprising way to replay <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/the-elder-scrolls-iii-morrowind">Morrowind</a>.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/morrowind-ds-mod">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Save-game carry-overs and time-leaping sequels: medieval vampire RPG The Blood of Dawnwalker has some bold ideas for the future</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/blood-of-dawnwalker-save-game-sequels</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 14:59:58 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/blood-of-dawnwalker-save-game-sequels</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>RPG</category><category>Story Rich</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Fantasy</category><category>Single Player</category><category>The Blood of Dawnwalker</category><category>Bioware</category><category>Rebel Wolves</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Open World</category><category>Mass Effect Trilogy Remastered</category><category>Shooter</category><category>RPG: Action</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Bandai Namco Entertainment</category><category>PS4</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Electronic Arts</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ambrus-dawnwalker.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/ambrus-dawnwalker.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>It's <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/mass-effect">Mass Effect</a> all over again, maybe. You'll be able to carry your save from The Blood of Dawnwalker into future Dawnwalker games, developer Rebel Wolves and publisher Bandai Namco have confirmed.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/blood-of-dawnwalker-save-game-sequels">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Modern Warfare 4 gameplay debut reignites community debate about how fast Call of Duty movement should be</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-gameplay-debut-community-reactions</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 14:36:27 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-gameplay-debut-community-reactions</guid><category>Modern Day</category><category>PC</category><category>Military</category><category>Square Enix</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Treyarch</category><category>PS5</category><category>Call of Duty: Black Ops 7</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Activision</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Realism</category><category>Raven Software</category><category>Infinity Ward</category><category>FPS</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>PS4</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4 (2026)</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/modern-warfare-4-soldiers-on-blue-background-1.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/modern-warfare-4-soldiers-on-blue-background-1.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Our first look at Modern Warfare 4 multiplayer gameplay arrived, <a href="https://www.vg247.com/events/call-of-duty-next">not as part of a Call of Duty: Next event, as is tradition</a>, but through a handful of livestreams from a select few who got to play the game at Fanatics Fest NYC, which took place 16th-19th July.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-modern-warfare-4-gameplay-debut-community-reactions">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>EA Sports FC simulations correctly predicted the FIFA World Cup winner would be Spain, and it's not the first time it has happened</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/ea-sports-fc-spain-winner-fifa-world-cup</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 13:53:47 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/ea-sports-fc-spain-winner-fifa-world-cup</guid><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>EA Sports FC 26</category><category>PC</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>PS4</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Third person</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Electronic Arts</category><category>EA Sports</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Simulation</category><category>Sports</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/EA-FC-26-Spain-team.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/EA-FC-26-Spain-team.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Spain is the new FIFA World Cup winner after defeating Argentina one to zero last night, and once again, the EA Sports FC game correctly predicted the result in advance.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/ea-sports-fc-spain-winner-fifa-world-cup">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>UK games retailer Game entered administration owing £16m, thanks to fierce competition, consumer trends, and "uncertainty associated with Brexit"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/uk-retailer-game-administration</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 13:35:25 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/uk-retailer-game-administration</guid><category>Blockbuster</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Game-Store.webp?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Game-Store.webp?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Insight into the fall of British high street video game retailer Game going into administration has been brought to light in a new report. After years of business troubles and challenges, this write-up claims the company's liquidation was caused by changing consumer behaviour, fierce competition, and "uncertainty associated with Brexit".</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/uk-retailer-game-administration">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"Honestly, it's still getting worse" - Valve Steam Machine engineer says component prices are still rising, potentially paving the way for a price increase</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/steam-machine-valve-component-price-increase</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:45:20 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/steam-machine-valve-component-price-increase</guid><category>PS6</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Steam Machine</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Valve</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/steam-machine-green.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/steam-machine-green.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>There is no end seemingly in sight for the memory crisis, or of how much higher the price of consumer electronics could go. Valve, which recently shipped its expensive Steam Machine, has learned this the hard way.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/steam-machine-valve-component-price-increase">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"Professional lurker" Todd Howard reappears on internet forums following Bethesda's Fallout and Elder Scrolls announcements to thank fans for their support</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/bethesda-todd-howard-reddit-lurker</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 12:29:02 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/bethesda-todd-howard-reddit-lurker</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>RPG</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>PS5</category><category>The Elder Scrolls VI</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bethesda Game Studios</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>PS4</category><category>Fallout 5</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Fallout 76</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Todd-Howard-at-Fallout-season-one-premier.-He-is-wearing-a-blue-suit-and-white-shirt-with-no-tie.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Todd-Howard-at-Fallout-season-one-premier.-He-is-wearing-a-blue-suit-and-white-shirt-with-no-tie.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Following <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/microsoft-xbox-layoffs-2026-double-fine-compulsion-ninja-theory">sweeping layoffs across the entire Xbox division</a> earlier this month, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/those-rumoured-fallout-3-and-fallout-new-vegas-remasteres-are-real-fallout-5-is-in-pre-production-and-fallout-76-is-getting-a-massive-expansion">Bethesda shared a surprisingly transparent roadmap about the Fallout and The Elder Scrolls projects</a> it's making. Now, <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/bethesda-game-studios">Bethesda Game Studios</a> leader <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/personas/todd-howard">Todd Howard</a> has returned to Reddit after a six-month hiatus to thank fans for their support.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/bethesda-todd-howard-reddit-lurker">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"The Gears of War trilogy was largely developed hungover by me" - Cliff Bleszinski reckons with a difficult past while plotting a return to games and a brighter future</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/cliff-bleszinski-alcoholism-gears-of-war-lawbreakers</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 10:44:28 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/cliff-bleszinski-alcoholism-gears-of-war-lawbreakers</guid><category>PC</category><category>LawBreakers</category><category>Gears of War 3</category><category>Xbox 360</category><category>Microsoft</category><category>Epic Games</category><category>Radical Heights</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Gears of War 2</category><category>Indie</category><category>First person</category><category>Boss Key Productions</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Nexon</category><category>Microsoft Studios</category><category>Gears of War</category><category>PS4</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Sports</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/cliff-bleszinski_ElyTLax.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/cliff-bleszinski_ElyTLax.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Cliff Bleszkinski, the designer instrumental in the creation of Gears of War - the face of the series for three games - has opened up about a career-long struggle with alcohol which he's now reckoning with, while also teasing a potential return to creating games.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/cliff-bleszinski-alcoholism-gears-of-war-lawbreakers">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Call of Duty voice chat lobbies turned into ASMR app that takes veterans back to the cacophonies of the MW2 and BO1 days</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-voice-chat-ambience-website</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Fran Ruiz</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 09:23:57 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-voice-chat-ambience-website</guid><category>Nintendo Wii U</category><category>PS3</category><category>PC</category><category>n-Space</category><category>Xbox 360</category><category>Square Enix</category><category>Treyarch</category><category>PS5</category><category>Call of Duty: Black Ops</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Nintendo Wii</category><category>Activision</category><category>Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 2 (2009)</category><category>Call of Duty: Black Ops 2</category><category>First person</category><category>Aspyr</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Activision Blizzard</category><category>Mac</category><category>Nintendo DS</category><category>PS4</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/bo_zStfFRs.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/bo_zStfFRs.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Whereas some people fall asleep to white noise or calm soundscapes, others can apparently do so while in the middle of noisy online matches. At least, that's what one app developer who was nostalgic for the olden Call of Duty days seems to think, as they have shaken the ASMR scene up with a lobby voice chat 'ambience' website.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-voice-chat-ambience-website">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced sold 3 million in its first week</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-resynced-3-million-copies-one-week</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 08:58:12 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-resynced-3-million-copies-one-week</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Ubisoft Entertainment</category><category>Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced</category><category>Ubisoft Montreal</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/AC-Black-Flag-Resynced-underwater-treasure.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/AC-Black-Flag-Resynced-underwater-treasure.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>After <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-resynced-2-million-sales">its big 2m sales opening</a>, Assassin's Creed Black Flag Resynced has reached a new sales milestone: Ubisoft announced that the remake has sold over 3m units in a week across all platforms.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/assassins-creed-black-flag-resynced-3-million-copies-one-week">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Kingdom Hearts Missing-Link may have been cancelled, but that hasn't stopped footage of Keyblade-wielding astronauts from leaking online</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/kingdom-hearts-missing-link-footage-leak-beyblade-astronauts</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Mon, 20 Jul 2026 08:48:51 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/kingdom-hearts-missing-link-footage-leak-beyblade-astronauts</guid><category>Square Enix</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Kingdom Hearts: Missing-Link</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>RPG</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Android</category><category>iOS</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kingdom-hearts-missing-link-keyblade-wielder.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kingdom-hearts-missing-link-keyblade-wielder.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Footage of the cancelled <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/kingdom-hearts">Kingdom Hearts</a> Missing-Link has appeared online, just over a year since development on the game ended.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/kingdom-hearts-missing-link-footage-leak-beyblade-astronauts">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Baldur's Gate 3, Clair Obscur actor Jennifer English withdraws from Tides of Annihilation to "look after her mental and physical health"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/jennifer-english-leaves-tides-of-annihilation</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 16:57:42 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/jennifer-english-leaves-tides-of-annihilation</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>RPG: Action</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Tides of Annihilation</category><category>Eclipse Glow</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Tides-of-Annihilation---Announce-Trailer-_-PS5-Games-0-23-screenshot.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Tides-of-Annihilation---Announce-Trailer-_-PS5-Games-0-23-screenshot.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The award-winning actor, Jennifer English, has withdrawn from Eclipse Glow Games' action game Tides of Annihilation to "look after [her] mental and physical health".</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/jennifer-english-leaves-tides-of-annihilation">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Game of Thrones: War for Westeros RTS delayed to 2027 to "ensure the game reaches the high level of quality we are aiming for"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/game-of-thrones-war-for-westeros-rts-game-delayed-to-2027</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 16:21:49 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/game-of-thrones-war-for-westeros-rts-game-delayed-to-2027</guid><category>Strategy: Real-Time Strategy</category><category>Game of Thrones</category><category>Playside Studios</category><category>PC</category><category>Historical</category><category>Fantasy</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Game Of Thrones: War For Westeros</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/game-of-thrones-war-for-westeros.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/game-of-thrones-war-for-westeros.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Bad news, Game of Thrones fans - PlaySide Studios' RTS based on the hugely successful book and TV series has been delayed to 2027.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/game-of-thrones-war-for-westeros-rts-game-delayed-to-2027">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Palworld is once again dominating Steam this weekend, clocking up almost 1m concurrent players</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-almost-hits-1-million-concurrents-again</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 15:51:45 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-almost-hits-1-million-concurrents-again</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>concurrent players</category><category>RPG</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><category>Open World</category><category>Indie</category><category>Palworld</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Mac</category><category>Pocketpair</category><category>MMORPG</category><category>PS4</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/palworld-grizzbolt-shooting-pals.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/palworld-grizzbolt-shooting-pals.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-beginner-tips-tricks-9409">Palworld</a> is once again one of the most played games on Steam this weekend.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/palworld-almost-hits-1-million-concurrents-again">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Call of Duty movie will be set in the Modern Warfare universe</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-movie-set-modern-warfare-universe</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 15:12:32 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-movie-set-modern-warfare-universe</guid><category>Modern Day</category><category>PC</category><category>Microsoft</category><category>Military</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Activision</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Realism</category><category>Infinity Ward</category><category>FPS</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Call of Duty: Modern Warfare III (2023)</category><category>Science Fiction</category><category>eSports relevant</category><category>PS4</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Call of Duty: Modern Warfare 4 (2026)</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/MW4_MP_003_BRANDED.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/MW4_MP_003_BRANDED.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>The upcoming Call of Duty movie will be set in the Modern Warfare universe.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/call-of-duty-movie-set-modern-warfare-universe">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Marathon director Joe Ziegler leaves Bungie just four months after launch</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/marathon-director-ziegler-leaves-bungie</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Vikki Blake</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 14:50:13 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/marathon-director-ziegler-leaves-bungie</guid><category>iOS</category><category>First person</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bungie</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Marathon</category><category>Mac</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/marathon-art-3.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/marathon-art-3.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Marathon director Joe Ziegler has left Bungie after three and a half years at the studio.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/marathon-director-ziegler-leaves-bungie">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Forbidden Solitaire is a wonderful reminder games are powerful cultural artefacts that demand to be preserved</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/forbidden-solitaire-90s-cd-rom-game-preservation</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Matt Wales</dc:creator><pubDate>Sun, 19 Jul 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/forbidden-solitaire-90s-cd-rom-game-preservation</guid><category>First person</category><category>Forbidden Solitaire</category><category>Visual Novel &amp; Dating</category><category>Puzzle</category><category>PC</category><category>Text</category><category>Strategy</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Now Playing</category><category>Night Signal Entertainment</category><category>Card Games</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/forbidden-solitaire-header-3.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/forbidden-solitaire-header-3.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Not so long ago, I found a stash of my old ZX Spectrum games in the attic. And rummaging through those tatty boxes - the old half-forgotten bargain bin bangers, the illicit passed-around-the-playground compilation tapes - it wasn't the games I found myself thinking about, it was the memories around them. My mind leapt back to evenings spent poring over stamp-sized magazine screenshots; the Friday night trips to Tescos and the exotic box art tempting me to part with my &pound;2; the POKE codes and the dog-eared anti-piracy sheets; the wild classroom rumours of in-game secrets that would only reveal themselves when elaborate steps were performed. But they're not just my memories, of course; they'll be familiar to many of a certain place and time. And it's this sense of cultural nostalgia that Forbidden Solitaire captures so well.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/forbidden-solitaire-90s-cd-rom-game-preservation">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Controversy-laden Disco Elysium and Zero Parades studio ZA/UM to lay off large chunk of staff once more</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/disco-elysium-zero-parades-studio-zaum-to-lay-off-large-chunk-of-staff-once-more</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Chris Tapsell</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 12:36:19 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/disco-elysium-zero-parades-studio-zaum-to-lay-off-large-chunk-of-staff-once-more</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>RPG</category><category>Story Rich</category><category>Mystery</category><category>PS5</category><category>Text</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Disco Elysium: The Final Cut</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Indie</category><category>Disco Elysium</category><category>Zero Parades: For Dead Spies</category><category>Exploration</category><category>ZA/UM</category><category>Mac</category><category>PS4</category><category>Stadia</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/zero-parades-layoffs-header-man-in-chair.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/zero-parades-layoffs-header-man-in-chair.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>ZA/UM Studio, the contentious developer at the heart of years of bitter public and legal disputes since the release of 2019's acclaimed <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/disco-elysium">Disco Elysium</a>, is to lay off up to 32 staff members "across all departments", it's been announced.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/disco-elysium-zero-parades-studio-zaum-to-lay-off-large-chunk-of-staff-once-more">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The full Blood of Dawnwalker game will be released on disc, Bandai Namco and Rebel Wolves confirm</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/blood-of-dawnwalker-released-on-disc</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 10:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/blood-of-dawnwalker-released-on-disc</guid><category>Story Rich</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Bandai Namco Entertainment</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Fantasy</category><category>RPG: Action</category><category>Single Player</category><category>The Blood of Dawnwalker</category><category>Rebel Wolves</category><category>RPG</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/brencis-danwalker-artwork.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/brencis-danwalker-artwork.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Promising new medieval vampire role-playing game The Blood of Dawnwalker will be, hallelujah, released on a good old fashioned disc.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/blood-of-dawnwalker-released-on-disc">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Netflix's games strategy might be a mess, but Oxenfree studio's ingenious new chiller-thriller shows it has a secret weapon</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/netflixs-games-strategy-might-be-a-mess-but-oxenfree-studios-ingenious-new-chiller-thriller-shows-it-has-a-secret-weapon</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Matt Wales</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 09:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/netflixs-games-strategy-might-be-a-mess-but-oxenfree-studios-ingenious-new-chiller-thriller-shows-it-has-a-secret-weapon</guid><category>Story Rich</category><category>Horror</category><category>PC</category><category>Walking Sim</category><category>Now Playing</category><category>Unhinged</category><category>iOS</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/unhinged-header_R5aN0Nb.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/unhinged-header_R5aN0Nb.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>I still vividly recall the moment in <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/no-more-heroes">No More Heroes</a> when my Wii Remote rang for the first time. Confusion turned to delight as I held the controller to my ear and, through its tiny tinny speaker, Sylvia began to speak, as if on the other end of the line. Suddenly, Travis Touchdown's world had broken free of the TV, and I was <em>thrilled</em>. Oxenfree developer Night School's brisk new horror game Unhinged, currently streaming on Netflix, is built from these kinds of fourth-wall-busting moments, helping turn an already breathless thriller into something fascinating.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/netflixs-games-strategy-might-be-a-mess-but-oxenfree-studios-ingenious-new-chiller-thriller-shows-it-has-a-secret-weapon">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Not so much James Bond, more Mission Impossible - 007 First Light was originally more of an ensemble piece, says IO Interactive</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/io-interactive-007-first-light-james-bond</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 08:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/io-interactive-007-first-light-james-bond</guid><category>IO Interactive</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>007 First Light</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/james-bond-007-first-light-cressida.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/james-bond-007-first-light-cressida.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/io-interactive">IO Interactive</a> once considered making 007 First Light more of an ensemble piece than it turned out to be. In other words, the game would have been less about James Bond on his own and more about him and a team of agents working together.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/io-interactive-007-first-light-james-bond">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>What we've been playing - "He takes great joy out of my suffering"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/what-weve-been-playing-he-takes-great-joy-out-of-my-suffering</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Sat, 18 Jul 2026 07:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/what-weve-been-playing-he-takes-great-joy-out-of-my-suffering</guid><category>PS3</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>2K Games</category><category>Xbox 360</category><category>ZeniMax Media</category><category>RPG</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><category>IO Interactive</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Irrational Games</category><category>Bethesda Game Studios</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>First person</category><category>Shooter</category><category>What we've been playing</category><category>BioShock Infinite: Burial At Sea Episode 1</category><category>Mac</category><category>007 First Light</category><category>The Elder Scrolls III: Morrowind</category><category>PS4</category><category>Ubisoft</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Xbox</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/emperor-palpatine.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/emperor-palpatine.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Hello and welcome back to our regular feature where we write a little about the games we've been playing. This week, Connor is expertly trolled by his friend and shares a controversial take on a game some people will love; Chris revisits an all-timer while remembering a time when it didn't seem so; and Bertie ruins a game for himself.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/what-weve-been-playing-he-takes-great-joy-out-of-my-suffering">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"I feel totally unbothered" - Deborah Ann Woll doesn't care about the trolls taking shots at God Of War Laufey</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-laufey-deborah-ann-woll-unbothered</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:42:02 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-laufey-deborah-ann-woll-unbothered</guid><category>God of War Laufey</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/laufey-sword.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/laufey-sword.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Since it was announced at the beginning of June, God of War Laufey has been receiving an unexpected amount of negative criticism. And a lot of the commentary about the game - of which we've only seen one trailer so far - revolves around the actress playing the eponymous character Laufey in it: Deborah Ann Woll, who reprises the role from God of War (2018).</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-laufey-deborah-ann-woll-unbothered">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Battlefield 6 is getting an evolved Carrier Assault mode in Season 4, and the Top Gun collab brings more than cosmetics</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-top-gun-collaboration-season-4-carrier-strike</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Sherif Saed</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 15:00:00 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-top-gun-collaboration-season-4-carrier-strike</guid><category>First person</category><category>PS5</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>Electronic Arts</category><category>Battlefield 6</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/battlefield-6-season-4-gameplay-screen-4.jpeg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/battlefield-6-season-4-gameplay-screen-4.jpeg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/battlefield-2025">Battlefield 6</a>'s upcoming Season 4 continues to look like one of its most exciting seasons yet. After <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-season-4-reveal-trailer-new-jets-top-gun-tease">delivering a first look at naval combat earlier this week</a>, Battlefield Studios has now detailed more of what we can expect throughout the season, including early details on the teased Top Gun collaboration.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/battlefield-6-top-gun-collaboration-season-4-carrier-strike">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Bethesda reassures fans The Elder Scrolls 6 is "on the way" following the Xbox cuts, and that it's "loving how it looks" and "playing it every day"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/elder-scrolls-6-xbox-layoffs-bethesda-reaction</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 14:48:48 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/elder-scrolls-6-xbox-layoffs-bethesda-reaction</guid><category>First person</category><category>Xbox Game Studios</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PC</category><category>The Elder Scrolls VI</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bethesda Game Studios</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/TGS6.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/TGS6.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/bethesda-game-studios">Bethesda Game Studios</a> has moved to calm concerns about The Elder Scrolls 6 following recent Xbox cuts, telling players that, "The next chapter is on the way. We're where we planned to be, loving how it looks, and playing it every day."</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/elder-scrolls-6-xbox-layoffs-bethesda-reaction">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Starfield "remains an important part of our future" says Bethesda, as developer pledges continued support for sci-fi RPG</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/starfield-impotant-part-of-future-bethesda-future-support</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 14:47:49 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/starfield-impotant-part-of-future-bethesda-future-support</guid><category>First person</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Science Fiction</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Starfield</category><category>Bethesda Game Studios</category><category>FPS</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/STARFIELD-SITE_aiZ8Li5.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/STARFIELD-SITE_aiZ8Li5.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Bethesda has confirmed that its spacefaring sci-fi RPG <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/starfield-main-story-walkthrough-9352">Starfield</a> will continue to be supported by the developer, even after suffering layoffs and has refocused on core franchises like The Elder Scrolls and Fallout.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/starfield-impotant-part-of-future-bethesda-future-support">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Those rumoured Fallout 3 and Fallout New Vegas remasters are real, Fallout 5 is in pre-production, and Fallout 76 is getting a massive expansion</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/those-rumoured-fallout-3-and-fallout-new-vegas-remasteres-are-real-fallout-5-is-in-pre-production-and-fallout-76-is-getting-a-massive-expansion</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 14:36:02 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/those-rumoured-fallout-3-and-fallout-new-vegas-remasteres-are-real-fallout-5-is-in-pre-production-and-fallout-76-is-getting-a-massive-expansion</guid><category>PS3</category><category>First person</category><category>Fallout: New Vegas</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Bandai Namco Entertainment</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Apple</category><category>Fallout 5</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Bethesda Game Studios</category><category>Xbox 360</category><category>Fallout 3</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><category>Obsidian Entertainment</category><category>iOS</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Fallout-3-nv.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Fallout-3-nv.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Bethesda has published a new statement which drops some major bombs (sorry) about the future of the Fallout series. <a href="https://bethesda.net/en/article/7wrffyXajE4BmCLJVpOkcN/a-note-from-bethesda-game-studios">In the statement</a>, the company noted that those long-rumoured <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/fallout-new-vegas">Fallout: New Vegas</a> and <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/fallout-3">Fallout 3</a> remasters are indeed real, teased a mystery Fallout project being developed with Obsidian, and - last but not least - announced that Fallout 5 is now in preproduction.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/those-rumoured-fallout-3-and-fallout-new-vegas-remasteres-are-real-fallout-5-is-in-pre-production-and-fallout-76-is-getting-a-massive-expansion">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Star Wars: KOTOR remake is alive and eyeing a 2028 release window, according to Sabre Interactive's chief business office</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/kotor-remake-2028-release-window-chief-business-officer</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 14:10:40 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/kotor-remake-2028-release-window-chief-business-officer</guid><category>Aspyr</category><category>PS5</category><category>Saber Interactive</category><category>PC</category><category>Lucasfilm Games</category><category>RPG</category><category>Embracer Group</category><category>Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic Remake</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kotor-remake-trailer-revan.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/kotor-remake-trailer-revan.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>It's no secret that the <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/star-wars-knights-of-the-old-republic">Star Wars: Knights of the Old Republic</a> (KOTOR) Remake has had its share of development woes, leaving many in dismay as one of the best Star Wars games of all time may never get its deserved polish-up. However, a recent message from Sabre Interactive's new chief business officer might offer a new hope (sorry).</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/kotor-remake-2028-release-window-chief-business-officer">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Claims about GTA 6 pre-orders are incorrect and "absurd", analyst firm says, but it's still had the "strongest pre-order campaign ever recorded"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-pre-order-numbers-record</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Dom Peppiatt</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 13:06:16 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-pre-order-numbers-record</guid><category>Grand Theft Auto VI</category><category>Modern Day</category><category>Shooter: Third Person</category><category>First person</category><category>Take-Two Interactive</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Rockstar Games</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Third person</category><category>Full product</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Racing</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/gta-boxed.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/gta-boxed.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>We all knew that <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-everything-we-know-so-far-9357">GTA 6</a> was going to be big, but new data from a video game market data analyst group suggests Rockstar's upcoming sandbox game has already earned in excess of $260m for the company.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-pre-order-numbers-record">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The new Marvel's Wolverine cinematic trailer has been swarmed by PlayStation fans still angry at Sony ditching discs</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/marvels-wolverine-story-trailer-sony-disc-outrage</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 11:14:54 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/marvels-wolverine-story-trailer-sony-disc-outrage</guid><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Insomniac Games</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Marvel's Wolverine</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/wolverine_riJvh67.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/wolverine_riJvh67.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>A cinematic trailer has been released for Insomniac Game's upcoming mutant action romp: Marvel's Wolverine. And while many fans have been excited to see another clawsome update for the game, it's been swarmed by those still angry at <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/sony-ending-playstation-discs-physical-media-january-2028">Sony's decision to ditch physical discs</a>.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/marvels-wolverine-story-trailer-sony-disc-outrage">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>No, Doom maker id Software hasn't been "nerfed into the ground and gutted" by the Xbox cuts, insists director Hugo Martin</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/id-software-xbox-cuts-doom</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 10:35:48 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/id-software-xbox-cuts-doom</guid><category>First person</category><category>PS5</category><category>Doom (2016)</category><category>Shooter</category><category>Horror</category><category>Doom Eternal</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>Doom: The Dark Ages</category><category>PC</category><category>PS4</category><category>id Software</category><category>FPS</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Stadia</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Bethesda Softworks</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/DOOM-SITE_5fKgryC-(1).jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/DOOM-SITE_5fKgryC-(1).jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Doom and Quake creator id Software insists it hasn't been "nerfed into the ground and gutted" by Xbox, despite reports to the contrary.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/id-software-xbox-cuts-doom">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>The live-action God of War TV series suffers a huge setback as Kratos actor is injured badly on set and needs to be recast</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-amazon-actor-ryan-hurst-injury-recast</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 09:06:01 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-amazon-actor-ryan-hurst-injury-recast</guid><category>Blockbuster</category><category>God of War</category><category>Amazon</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Kratos-in-God-of-War.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/Kratos-in-God-of-War.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Amazon's upcoming God of War TV show has hit a major obstacle after Kratos actor Ryan Hurst suffered a serious injury on set.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/god-of-war-amazon-actor-ryan-hurst-injury-recast">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>Castlevania Belmont's Curse could just be a gaming classic whipped back into shape</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/castlevania-belmonts-curse-preview</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Connor Makar</dc:creator><pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2026 07:00:23 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/castlevania-belmonts-curse-preview</guid><category>Motion Twin</category><category>Konami</category><category>Metroidvania</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>Evil Empire</category><category>PS5</category><category>PC</category><category>Nintendo Switch</category><category>Exploration</category><category>Platformer</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Side view</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>RPG</category><category>Hack &amp; Slash</category><category>Castlevania: Belmont’s Curse</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/0608_01.png?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/0608_01.png?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>Castlevania Belmont's Curse is a grand return to the series' platformer roots. Developed by Konami and Evil Empire, it's a gothic cathedral built with new material, upon the strongest of genre foundations. In the few hours I had to explore the game's opening act, I was quickly thrust into the classic Castlevania experience - battling against various enemies with a repertoire of weapons and magic - but there are some bold twists here that help differentiate this game from its ancestors.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/castlevania-belmonts-curse-preview">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"It has to make sense for the game" - EA sees a "huge opportunity" for in-game advertising "but it has to be done properly"</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/ea-in-game-advertising-opportunity</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Robert Purchese</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 15:49:34 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/ea-in-game-advertising-opportunity</guid><category>Maxis</category><category>PC</category><category>Bird view / Isometric</category><category>RPG</category><category>Simulation</category><category>Nintendo Switch 2</category><category>Life Simulation</category><category>PS5</category><category>Third person</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox One</category><category>The Sims 4</category><category>First person</category><category>EA Sports FC 27</category><category>The Sims Studio</category><category>Mac</category><category>PS4</category><category>Electronic Arts</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Sports</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/the-sims-coach-collab.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/the-sims-coach-collab.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p>It sounds as though EA's being careful, for now, about which brands can advertise in its games.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/ea-in-game-advertising-opportunity">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item><item><title>"It's not that we don't care about PC" - Former Rockstar developer suggests why GTA 6 is only coming to consoles at launch</title><link>https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-rockstar-pc-consoles-release</link><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Matt Wales</dc:creator><pubDate>Thu, 16 Jul 2026 13:11:51 +0000</pubDate><guid>https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-rockstar-pc-consoles-release</guid><category>Grand Theft Auto VI</category><category>Modern Day</category><category>Shooter: Third Person</category><category>First person</category><category>Take-Two Interactive</category><category>Action Adventure</category><category>PS5</category><category>Rockstar Games</category><category>Shooter</category><category>PC</category><category>Third person</category><category>Full product</category><category>Single Player</category><category>Xbox Series X/S</category><category>Multiplayer Cooperative</category><category>Racing</category><category>Multiplayer Competitive</category><category>Open World</category><media:content medium="image" url="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/gta-6-trailer-city.jpg?width=690&amp;quality=85&amp;format=jpg&amp;auto=webp"/><description><![CDATA[<img src="https://assetsio.gnwcdn.com/gta-6-trailer-city.jpg?width=690&quality=85&format=jpg&auto=webp" /> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-everything-we-know-so-far-9357">GTA 6</a> is looming like that monolith in 2001: A Space Odyssey, casting its fearsome shadow over the games industry and probably also scaring some monkeys. But PC players won't be able to join in the fun when <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/companies/rockstar-games">Rockstar Games</a>' mega-sequel launches on 19th November, and former studio producer John Ricchio - who worked on the likes of <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/grand-theft-auto-v">GTA 5</a>, Red Dead Redemption, and <a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/games/max-payne-3">Max Payne 3</a> - has shared some insight into why that may be.</p> <p><a href="https://www.eurogamer.net/gta-6-rockstar-pc-consoles-release">Read more</a></p>]]></description></item></channel></rss>